---
A XORN picket boat's recorder, still pinging for a ship that sank in here a long time ago.
Its nav log ends in this room.

## [Relics](relics)

### [The Sink](sink)
---
Atmosphere: purple
Containment: tractor
Scrape band: 200
Margin: 120
Forbid jump: yes
Seed: 113
Art: plain_asteroid_6, plain_asteroid_8, plain_asteroid_9
Walls: cave, rock
---
One room, flooded and enormous, with a hole in one end.

### [the inlet](inlet)
---
Relic: sink
Box: -3250, 0, 0, 1000, 350, 350
Scan: The only way in, and the only way out.
---
The hole in the end. It is the only way in and it is the only way out.

It has to OVERLAP the basin, not stop against it. At `-3300` with a half-extent of `900`
the inlet ended at x = -2400 and the basin began at x = -2400, so the two shared a plane
of zero thickness: a containment test sees one connected space, because a point on that
plane is inside both, but nothing can fly through a doorway with no width. The relic read
as flyable and the only way in was sealed.

### [the sink](basin)
---
Relic: sink
Box: 200, 0, 0, 2600, 900, 2600
Scan: Five kilometres of room, no floor plan at all, and murk you could stand on.
---
Five kilometres of room and no floor plan at all. Fly it however you like - there is
nothing in here that cares which way you came.

### [the drift](drift_solid)
---
Relic: sink
Solid: sphere, 200, 0, 0, 700
Dress: ruins_cv_rubble
---
A mass of settled debris hanging in the middle of the room, big enough to hide the far wall
from the near one.

