## [Dialogue](dialogue)

What the Sink's places say. See the Voice's file for how a place scene works.

### [The Near Side](sink_near_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% The Sink is one room, flooded with murk and enormous, and it has no floor plan at all: a drift of debris hangs in the middle, big enough to hide the far wall from the near one, and past it something long and dark lies right across the room.

- [Take a sounding](sink_sounding) if science ; check science 7 else sink_sounding_mud, signal sink_sounding_taken
- [Pick a line past the drift](sink_line) if helm ; check helm 7 else sink_line_lost, signal sink_line_found
- [Listen to the murk](sink_listen) if comms ; check comms 8 else sink_listen_nothing, reveal sink_wreck, signal sink_wreck_found
- [Move on]()

### [Sorted by Weight](sink_sounding)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% Everything in here drifted in through the inlet and never drifted out - a thousand years of it, sorted by weight. The heaviest things are all on the far side.

- [Log it]()

### [Mud](sink_sounding_mud)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% The sounding comes back as mud, and more mud.

- [Try again](sink_near_look)
- [Move on]()

### [A Lane](sink_line)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% A lane through the murk, past the drift on its low side, marked by nothing but the suit's own count.

- [Mark it]()

### [Turned Round](sink_line_lost)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% The murk turns the suit round twice before you notice. Start again from the inlet.

- [Try again](sink_near_look)
- [Move on]()

### [A Locator](sink_listen)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% A locator, weak and slow, from near the long dark thing across the room - a flight recorder, still pinging for a ship that sank in here a long time ago.

- [Mark it]()

### [Hiss](sink_listen_nothing)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% Hiss, and the murk ticking against the suit.

- [Listen again](sink_near_look)
- [Move on]()

### [The Picket Boat](sink_wreck_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% A small hull, crushed against the wrack and half buried in settled murk. Its recorder is still pinging. The hull markings are XORN's.

- [Read the markings](sink_wreck_marks) if weapons ; check weapons 7 else sink_wreck_blur, signal sink_marks_read
- [Reel the recorder in]()

### [Lost in the Chase](sink_wreck_marks)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% A XORN picket boat, lost in here chasing somebody - the plot on its nav log ends in this room. Whoever they were chasing got out again.

- [Tell Storm](sink_wreck_storm)

### [Storm, on the Picket](sink_wreck_storm)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% XORN, chasing somebody through a flooded ruin a long time before we ever heard of the Beacon? Then they have been on this trail longer than I have. Bring the recorder. I want the rest of that plot.

- [Understood]()

### [Scoured](sink_wreck_blur)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% The murk has scoured the hull markings to shadows.

- [Look again](sink_wreck_look)
- [Reel the recorder in]()

### [The Far Side](sink_far_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% Behind the drift: the far side, and the heaviest of everything that ever settled here, heaped against the wall. A haul, if anyone can shift it.

- [Tell Eddy what you have found](sink_far_eddy) if comms
- [Move on]()

### [Eddy, on the Haul](sink_far_eddy)
---
Speaker: crazy_eddy
---
% A thousand years of drift and nobody has picked it over? Take all of it. Empty that room. I will empty my till.

- [We'll see]()

